    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d603">

                <pb facs="0652" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg640"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/7960: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-27T22:00:00+02:00">January 27,
                            1941—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 28—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>126. My 102, January 22, 7 p.m.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d603-f1"/> According to
                    source heretofore reliable, the only definite decision reached at the
                    Berchtesgaden meeting<anchor n="14" xml:id="d603-f2"/> was for German military
                    support in Albania to ensure prompt and successful conclusion of war against
                    Greece. Strong counteroffensive to be launched soon as weather permits; large
                    numbers Italian troops being called for service Albania, and German soldiers
                    already on way to Italian embarkation ports.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>The reference to German military support in Albania is unexpected as our
                    information up to now has been that German intervention in that sector was
                    unlikely.</p>
                <pb facs="0653" n="641" xml:id="pg641"/>
                <p>Military Attaché is cabling on reported arrival during last few days of two
                    divisions German troops.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
